        },
        "responses": {
          "values": [
            {
              "content": "=You are an API reliability engineer.\n\nAnalyze the current API test incident together with the recent monitoring history.\n\nCURRENT TEST RESULT\n\nTest name: {{ $(\"Save Test Result\").first().json.test_name }}\nService: {{ $(\"Save Test Result\").first().json.service_name }}\nURL: {{ $(\"Save Test Result\").first().json.tested_url }}\n\nResult: {{ $(\"Save Test Result\").first().json.result }}\n\nHTTP status:\nActual: {{ $(\"Save Test Result\").first().json.status_code }}\nExpected: {{ $(\"Save Test Result\").first().json.expected_status }}\nStatus passed: {{ $(\"Save Test Result\").first().json.status_passed }}\n\nResponse time: {{ $(\"Save Test Result\").first().json.response_time }} ms\nMaximum allowed response time: {{ $(\"Save Test Result\").first().json.max_response_time }} ms\nResponse time passed: {{ $(\"Save Test Result\").first().json.response_time_passed }}\n\nRequired fields passed: {{ $(\"Save Test Result\").first().json.required_fields_passed }}\nMissing fields: {{ JSON.stringify($(\"Save Test Result\").first().json.missing_fields) }}\n\nExpected values passed: {{ $(\"Save Test Result\").first().json.expected_values_passed }}\nIncorrect values: {{ JSON.stringify($(\"Save Test Result\").first().json.incorrect_values) }}\n\nResponse structure passed: {{ $(\"Save Test Result\").first().json.response_structure_passed }}\n\n\nRECENT MONITORING HISTORY\n\nResults analyzed: {{ $json.analyzedResults }}\n\nPASS count: {{ $json.passCount }}\nWARNING count: {{ $json.warningCount }}\nFAIL count: {{ $json.failCount }}\n\nAverage response time: {{ $json.averageResponseTime }} ms\nLatest response time: {{ $json.latestResponseTime }} ms\n\nRecent incidents: {{ $json.recentIncidents }}\n\nTrend: {{ $json.trend }}\nLatest result: {{ $json.latestResult }}\nLatest test time: {{ $json.latestTestedAt }}\n\n\nANALYSIS\n\nProvide:\n\n1. Short diagnosis\nExplain what failed in the current API test.\n\n2. Most likely cause\nIdentify the most probable technical or configuration cause.\n\n3. Severity\nClassify the incident as:\nLOW, MEDIUM, HIGH, or CRITICAL.\n\nTake the monitoring history and trend into account when determining severity.\n\n4. Trend assessment\nExplain whether the API appears STABLE or DEGRADING based on recent monitoring results.\n\n5. Recommended actions\nProvide concise and practical steps to investigate or resolve the issue.\n\nKeep the response concise, technical, and practical."
            }
          ]
        },
